          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em Azumaya algebra
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+unital+ring"} commutative unital ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            that has an inverse up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an Azumaya algebra if there is an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \otimes_R A
            is Morita equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            form a group, which is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#traditional Traditional
          %p
            In what follows,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+unital+ring"} commutative unital ring
            and algebras over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            are assumed associative and unital but not necessarily commmutative. An
            %strong Azumaya algebra
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            obeying any of the following equivalent conditions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                There exists an
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                such that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                of
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \otimes_R A
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalent
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\mathrm{op}} \otimes_R A
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalent
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\mathrm{op}}
                is the opposite algebra of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} center
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+algebra"} separable algebra
            %li
              %p
                As a left
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                finitely generated, faithful and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi End
                        %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\otimes_R A^{op}\to End_R(A)
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a field, an Azumaya algebra is the same as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+simple+algebra"} central simple algebra
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            For any commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+bicategory"} monoidal bicategory
            with
          %ul
            %li
              algebras over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              as objects,
            %li bimodules as morphisms,
            %li bimodule homomorphisms as 2-morphisms.
          %p
            Given any monoidal bicategory we can take its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-group"} 3-group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+3-group"} Picard 3-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Azumaya+algebras"} Azumaya algebras
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            as its objects.
          %h3#over_a_scheme Over a scheme
          %p
            More generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            defines an
            %strong Azumaya algebra
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_x
            is an Azumaya
            = succeed "-algebra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X,x}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(X)
            classifies Azumaya algebras over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            up to a suitably defined equivalence relation:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}\sim\mathcal{B}
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℬ
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_X} \mathbf{End}(\mathcal{E}) \cong \mathcal{B}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_X}\mathbf{End}(\mathcal{F})
            for some locally free sheaves of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            of finite rank. The group operation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(X)
            is induced by the tensor product. The Brauer group can be reexpressed in terms of second
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            determines an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X^*
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            (or
            = succeed "-gerbe" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            context).
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+K-theory"} Karoubi K-theory
            involves an element in a Brauer group and in the original Karoubi–Donovan paper is related to a twisting with a “local system” which involves Azumaya algebras.
          %h3#InTermsOfEtaleCohomology In terms of (derived) étale cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n_{et}(-,-)
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+cohomology"} etale cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi et
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔾
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0_{et}(R, \mathbb{G}_m) = R^\times
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"}> group of units
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi et
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔾
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi Pic
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1_{et}(R, \mathbb{G}_m) = Pic(R)
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+group"}> Picard group
                \: iso classes of invertible
                = succeed "-modules)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi et
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔾
                        %mi m
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi tor
                      %mo =
                      %mi Br
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{et}(R, \mathbb{G}_m)_{tor} = Br(R)
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
                Morita classes of Azumaya
                = succeed "-algebras)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            More generally, this works for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a (connective)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            (the following is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Antieau"} Benjamin Antieau
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(R)
            be its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group+of+units"} infinity-group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postikov stage
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+group"} Picard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pic
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Pic(R) \coloneqq Mod(R)^\times
          %p is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi et
                          %msub
                            %mi GL
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Pic
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}_{et} GL_1(-) &amp;\to&amp; Pic(-)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{Z}
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the top morphism is the inclusion of locally free
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1_{et}(R, GL_1)
            is not equal to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi Pic
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 Pic(R)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi components
                        %mi of
                        %mi R
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0_{et}(R, \mathbb{Z}) = \prod_{components of R} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} modules
          %p
            There is a notion of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} enriched (infinity,1)-category
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-categories\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi R
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_R \coloneqq Mod_R
            \-modiles in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} presentable (infinity,1)-categories
          %p
            Forming module
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi R
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mod
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Alg_R \stackrel{Mod}{\to} Cat_R
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi R
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Car
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat'_R \hookrightarrow Car_R
            for the image of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi R
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Br(R) \coloneqq (Cat'_R)^\times
          %p
            One shows (Antieau-Gepner) that this is exactly the Azumaya
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (B. Antieau, D. Gepner)
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                a connective
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
                ring, any Azumaya
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is étale locally trivial: there is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topology"} etale cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to S
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi R
                        %mi S
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi Morita
                            %mo ≃
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \wedge_R S \stackrel{Morita \simeq}{\to} S
              %p
                (Think of this as saying that an Azumaya
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "-2-bundle)." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi GL
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(R)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Br
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi CAlg
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Gpd
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br : CAlg_R^{\geq 0} \to Gpd_\infty
                is a sheaf for the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+cohomology"} etale cohomology
          %p
            %strong Corollary
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Br
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Br
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi et
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi Br
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br \simeq \mathbf{B}_{et} \Omega Br
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Br
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Pic
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega Br \simeq Pic
                , hence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Br
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi et
                      %mi Pic
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br \simeq \mathbf{B}_{et} Pic
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(R)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi for
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  for\; n \gt 0: \pi_n GL_1(S) \simeq \pi_n
          %p
            hence for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to S
            étale
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_n S \simeq \pi_n R \otimes_{\pi_0 R} \pi_0 S
          %p
            This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-coherent+sheaf"} quasi-coherent sheaf
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 R
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde N
            (quasicoherent sheaf associated with a module), for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            an
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ;
                  %mi for
                  %mi p
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_{et}^1(\pi_0 R, \tilde N) = 0; for p \gt 0
          %p
            For every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"} (infinity,1)-sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi R
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi q
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo −
                      %mi p
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_{et}^p(\pi_0 R; \tilde \pi_q G) \Rightarrow \pi_{q-p} G(R)
          %p
            (the second argument on the left denotes the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi qth
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} qth
            Postnikov stage). From this one gets the following.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 0
                      %mi Br
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \pi_0 Br \simeq *
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 1
                      %mi Br
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \pi_1 Br \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 2
                      %mi Br
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 1
                      %mi Pic
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi GL
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔾
                        %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \pi_2 Br \simeq \tilde \pi_1 Pic \simeq \pi_0 GL_1 \simeq \mathbb{G}_m
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mi n
                      %mi Br
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \pi_n Br
                is quasicoherent for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 2
          %p
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to
                  H_{et}^2(\pi_0 R, \mathbb{G}_m)
                  \\to \pi_0 Br(R)
                  \\to H_{et}^1(\pi_0 R, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\to 0
          %p
            (notice the inclusion
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(\pi_0 R) \hookrightarrow H_{et}^2(\pi_0 R, \mathbb{G}_m)
          %p
            this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} split exact
            and so computes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 Br(R)
            for connective
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            Now some more on the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is not connective.
          %p
            Suppose there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \stackrel{\phi}{\to} S
            which is a faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+extension"} Galois extension
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
          %p
            %strong Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                (real into complex
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+spectrum"} K-theory spectrum
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi KO
                      %mo →
                      %mi KU
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO \to KU
                (this is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                      %mi tmf
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to tmf(3)
          %p
            Give
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi fib
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Pic
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi fib
                  %mi Pic
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Pic
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi fib
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Gl_1(R/S) \stackrel{fib}{\to} GL_1(R) \to GL_1(S)
                  \\to
                  Pic(R/S) \stackrel{fib}{\to} Pic(R) \to Pic(S)
                  \\to
                  Br(R/S) \stackrel{fib}{\to} Br(R) \to Br(S) \to \cdots
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (descent theorems) (Tyler Lawson, David Gepner) Given
            = succeed "-Galois" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi hG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} S^{hG}
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+points"}> homotopy fixed points
            )
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi S
                        %mi hG
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Mod_S^{hG}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Alg
                        %mi S
                        %mi hG
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_R \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Alg_S^{hG}
          %p it follows that there is a homotopy fixed points spectral sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^p(G, \pi_\bullet \Sigma^n GL_1(S))
                  \\Rightarrow
                  \\pi_{-n} GL_1(S)
          %p
            %strong Conjecture
            The spectral sequence gives an Azumaya
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KO
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            which is a nontrivial element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi KO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(KO)
            but becomes trivial in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Br
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi KU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Br(KU)
          %h3#azumaya_categories Azumaya categories
          %p
            Borceux and Vitale have noted that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+bicategory"} monoidal bicategory
            of
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory, leading to a concept of “Azumaya category”. An Azumaya algebra over the commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is then a one-object Azumaya category enriched over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
          %p
            More precisely, they consider an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benabou+cosmos"} Benabou cosmos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete"} complete
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete"} cocomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed
            category. This gives a monoidal bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Mod
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-enriched categories as objects,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
              as morphisms, and
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-natural transformations between
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of this monoidal bicategory is a 3-group, and they call the objects of the core
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Azumaya categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"} Enrico Vitale
              %em Applied Categorical Structures
              %strong 10
              (2002), 449-467. (
              %a{:href => "https://perso.uclouvain.be/enrico.vitale/Azumaya.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"}> group of units
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+group"} Picard group
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+3-group"} Picard 3-group
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+C-star-algebra"}> homogeneous C-star-algebra
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous-trace+algebra"} continuous-trace algebra
            %li
              special case:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+simple+algebra"} central simple algebra
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://mate.dm.uba.ar/~gcorti"}> G. Cortiñas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"} Charles Weibel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homology of Azumaya algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 121
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/2160364"} jstor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Duskin"}> John Duskin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Azumaya complex of a commutative ring
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0081352"} doi:10.1007/BFb0081352
            %li#GrothendieckBrauer
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Le groupe de Brauer I, II, III
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Donovan"} Peter Donovan
                %em
                  Graded Brauer groups and
                  = succeed "-theory" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                (
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/ARCHIVE/PMIHES/PMIHES_1970__38_/PMIHES_1970__38__5_0/PMIHES_1970__38__5_0.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                M-A. Knus, M. Ojanguren,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Théorie de la descente et algèbres d’Azumaya
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 389
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1007/BFb0057799"} doi:10.1007/BFb0057799
            %li
              %p
                J. Milne,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Étale cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Descent
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.mq.edu.au/~street/Descent.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some combinatorial aspects of descent theory
                %strong 12
                (2004) 537-576,
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0303175"} math.CT/0303175
                (sec. 12, Brower groups)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"}> Enrico Vitale
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Picard-Brauer exact sequence of categorical groups
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucl.ac.be/membres/vitale/cat-gruppi2.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Ana-L. Agore,
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Stefan Caenepeel
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Stefan+Caenepeel"} ?
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braidings on the category of bimodules, Azumaya algebras and epimorphisms of rings
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-012-9294-3"} doi
          %p
            The observation that passing to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            makes also the non-torsion elements in the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigger+Brauer+group"}> bigger Brauer group
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{et}(-,\mathbb{G}_m)
            be represented by (derived) Azumaya algebras is due to
          %ul
            %li#Toen10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                %em Derived Azumaya algebras and generators for twisted derived categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.2599"}> arXiv:1002.2599
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Artin"}> Michael Artin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Azumaya algebras and finite-dimensional representations of rings
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 11
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(69)90091-X"} doi
          %p
            The comparison of the Artin’s theorem on characterization of Azumaya algebras and Tomiyama-Takesaki’s theorem on
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+C%2A-algebra"} homogeneous C*-algebra
          %ul
            %li
              Edward Formanek,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative invariant theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 43
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/043"} doi
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azumaya_algebra"} Azumaya algebra
            %li
              %p
                Urs Schreiber,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/string/archives/000786.html"} Picard and Brauer 2-groups
            %li
              %p
                John Baez,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2020/05/the_brauer_3group.html"} The Brauer 3-group
                = succeed "-Category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
